  "content": {
    "id": "p46-q54-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Which of the following sets are equal?\n$$\\begin{aligned}X&=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R\\text{ where }x^2=16\\}\\\\Y&=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R\\text{ where }x+4=0\\}\\\\Z&=\\{4,-4\\}\\end{aligned}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$X=Z$",
      "worked": "$(-4)^2=16$ and $4^2=16$, while $x+4=0$ gives $x=-4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}X&=\\{-4,4\\}\\\\Y&=\\{-4\\}\\\\Z&=\\{4,-4\\}\\end{align*}$$\nThus $X=Z$, because order does not affect equality of sets. $Y$ does not contain 4.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
